       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg in one dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon regimens are:\n- 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day. For example, 800 mg three times daily is 2,400 mg/day.\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours for mild to moderate pain or fever, which is 1,600 mg/day.\n\nYou might have meant 1600 mg total per day, such as 400 mg four times daily. Or you might have meant 800 mg QID, which is the 3,200 mg/day maximum.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg QID, please confirm that it's intentional and give me a note for the order. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
