       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you've confirmed it and are taking responsibility. But 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any adult indication for it. The risk of serious harm is high, mainly GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Your confirmation doesn't change that risk to the patient, so I'm not comfortable placing it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg PO four times daily:** 1,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the maximum, I'd suggest calling pharmacy or the attending to discuss it. You could also consider another analgesic or adding one, such as scheduled acetaminophen. Let me know which option you'd like, and I'll enter it."
